  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Why do you only call your mom when you're walking somewhere?",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 2.5
    },
    {
      "text": "You put your shoes on, step outside, and suddenly you've got ten minutes and a lot to say.",
      "start": 3.16,
      "end": 7.64
    },
    {
      "text": "And it's because a walk gives the call an ending, so you can always say I'm here, got to go.",
      "start": 7.94,
      "end": 13.26
    },
    {
      "text": "So when it's going well, you take the long way round the block.",
      "start": 14.04,
      "end": 17.2
    },
    {
      "text": "And she knows, because she always saves the big news for the last street.",
      "start": 17.66,
      "end": 21.66
    }
  ],
